  "analytical_usefulness": 0.78,
  "source_groundedness": 0.8,
  "rationale": "The added columns give several genuine analytical axes (completion gap, progress ratio, duration, on-track flag) directly relevant to what signals a highly achieved goal, all derivable from the original percentage and date fields. priority_score and high_achievement_score are partly redundant restatements, but still add mild leverage. Values are soundly grounded in the source columns; occasional anomalies (negative durations, inconsistent composite weighting) reflect data/logic quirks rather than invented facts, so no clear hallucination."
